.env
.venv/

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# `prompts/` stays out of this repository entirely (phase 0W).
#
# The judgement that produced the old exception here is unchanged: the batch
# reports and DECISIONS.md are **not** byproducts, and they remain the only
# record of why the code is the way it is. What changed is where that record
# lives. This repository is becoming public, and the working record — briefs
# written to an agent, reports written back, and a decision log that names
# people and unfinished judgements — is not something to publish by default.
#
# So the reports are still written, as files, exactly as before. They are kept
# outside this repository. See CLAUDE.md, "Where the working record goes".
prompts/

# Run artifacts: raw API responses, metrics, previews. Regenerable, often large.
# Labels are the exception — a human made them and they cannot be regenerated.
runs/*
!runs/labels/
runs/labels/*_pool.jsonl

# Subscriber addresses are personal data and must never reach a commit. First,
# so that nothing below can accidentally re-include them (phase 0k, X5-3).
subscribers/
*.subscribers
UC_PREVIEW_RECIPIENT

# The built site. Regenerable from `content/` by `uc site` in under a second,
# and rebuilt on every run — committing it would put a large diff of derived
# HTML in front of every real change. `docs/design-review.html` is the same
# thing wearing a different name (phase 0k, X0-4).
#
# If a deploy is ever wired up it publishes from a build step, not from a
# committed directory; §X6 records that decision.
site/
docs/design-review.html

# Trained models ARE committed (hotfix H1). They were ignored as "build outputs"
# and that reasoning was wrong twice over:
#
#   - `classify` does not degrade without one. `latest_model_path()` raises
#     FileNotFoundError when the pinned version is missing, on purpose, so a
#     clean checkout fails the stage every time. CI failed on YJUN's very first
#     run for exactly this.
#   - They are 4KB each. Logistic regression over embeddings is weights and
#     nothing else; all five together are 20KB. Calling that a build artefact
#     cost more than storing it ever will.
#
# Reproducible and deployable are different properties. The training metadata in
# models/*.json makes them reproducible; committing the joblib makes them
# present. Being able to rebuild a thing is not a reason to ship without it.

# Local embedding cache
.cache/
